/*!
\page page_stgmthit StGmtHit

\brief One-dimensional cluster (hit) in a GMT module, providing local X/Y position and ADC charge.

\section gmthit_overview Overview

StGmtHit is a 1D cluster in the **GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)** — the GMT analogue
of StFgtHit.  It stores the ADC sums and local positions in both X (strip) and Y (pad)
directions for a single module cluster, along with position uncertainties and a unique key.

**Detector**: GEM-based Muon Tracker (GMT)  
**Stage**: Strip clustering → 1D cluster position

\section gmthit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\code
TObject → StObject → StHit → StGmtHit
\endcode

Stored in the GMT hit container within \c StGmtCollection.

\section gmthit_coordinates Coordinate Convention

The module index is stored as \c mHardwarePosition = module + 1.
- \c mPosition.x() / \c getLocalX(): position along X-strips (cm)
- \c mPosition.y() / \c getLocalY(): position along Y-pads (cm)
- \c mSigmaX / \c mSigmaY: alternative position estimates

\section gmthit_members Data Members

| Type | Member | Description |
|------|--------|-------------|
| \c Int_t | \c mKey | Unique cluster ID |
| \c Float_t | \c mAdcX, \c mAdcY | Integrated ADC charge in X and Y |
| \c Float_t | \c mdAdcX, \c mdAdcY | ADC charge uncertainties |
| \c Float_t | \c mSigmaX, \c mErrSigmaX | Alternative X position and its uncertainty |
| \c Float_t | \c mSigmaY, \c mErrSigmaY | Alternative Y position and its uncertainty |

Inherited \c mPosition.x()/y() holds the primary local X/Y; \c mPositionError.x()/y() holds uncertainties.

\section gmthit_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| \c getKey() | Unique cluster ID |
| \c getModule() | Module index (0–7) |
| \c getAdcX(), \c getAdcY() | ADC charge sums |
| \c getLocalX(), \c getLocalY() | Local position (cm) |
| \c getErrorLocalX(), \c getErrorLocalY() | Position uncertainties |
| \c getSigmaX(), \c getSigmaY() | Alternative position estimates |

\section gmthit_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
const StGmtHit* hit = hitColl->hit(ih);
int   mod  = hit->getModule();    // 0-7
float x    = hit->getLocalX();    // cm
float y    = hit->getLocalY();    // cm
float adcX = hit->getAdcX();
\endcode

\see StGmtStrip, StGmtPoint, StGmtCollection
*/
